  data: {
    LLM: "Count trumps (there are 8). When you have the 'Master' (Jack), draw trumps out immediately. Don't bid unless you have at least the Jack or the 9-Ace combo.\n\nThe 'Impasse' (Finesse): Leading a low card through the opponent to trap their King/Queen if your partner holds the Ace/10. Trapping the 10 is crucial as it's worth 10 points.\n\nSignaling (Appel): Discarding an Ace on a partner's winning trick signals 'I have the 10 or King, lead this suit again'. Or discarding a 7 asks for a suit change.",
    Player: "Count trumps (there are 8). When you have the 'Master' (Jack), draw trumps out immediately. Don't bid unless you have at least the Jack or the 9-Ace combo.\n\nThe 'Impasse' (Finesse): Leading a low card through the opponent to trap their King/Queen if your partner holds the Ace/10. Trapping the 10 is crucial as it's worth 10 points.\n\nSignaling (Appel): Discarding an Ace on a partner's winning trick signals 'I have the 10 or King, lead this suit again'. Or discarding a 7 asks for a suit change.",
